      {
        "id": 246442,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-07-15T22:09:41.790Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Risky Actions are generally equivalent to a Green ability, so the first of those is fine, and the third is probably fine even at a Mid die (using the Minion-Maker table, otherwise it’s too random).</p>\n<p>I’m not as crazy about allowing unlimited Recover for anyone at any time.  It’s probably not “unbalanced” but it’s bad for game flow given the rest of the game’s design.</p>\n<p>The other problem is complexity.  Opening up that many possible Risky Actions adds a lot of possibility space, so if players are thinking about too many options all the time, things could bog down.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-07-15T22:09:41.790Z",
