      {
        "id": 247310,
        "name": "Chief Lackey Rich",
        "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2022-08-14T16:21:30.969Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"29487\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In actual practice, though, I think I’d probably only offer these to my players if they specifically asked for a way to do one of them.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Seems sensible.  That’s my usual approach on all Risky Actions anyway, and none of these new ideas look overly strong.  I might worry a bit about bigfooting another hero’s schtick if they were getting used a lot - eg if you have a Minion-Maker hero, be careful of letting other folks make them with risky actions too often, or if you have a hero built to do healing be careful about allowing risky Recoveries - but odds are it won’t be an issue.  A “risky minion” is going to be pretty weak compared to what a real MM’s minions can do, so less impetus to bother taking the twist for one, and similarly a healer should be able to handle playing medic.</p>",
